.TH PTRACE 2 "2026-02-28" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
ptrace \- process trace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/ptrace.h>
.PP
.BI "long ptrace(int " request ", pid_t " pid ", void *" addr ", void *" data ");"
.SH LIBRARY
System call library
.RI ( libsys ", " \-lsys )
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR ptrace ()
system call provides a means by which one process (the "tracer") may
observe and control the execution of another process (the "tracee"),
and examine and change the tracee's memory and registers.  It is
primarily used to implement breakpoint debugging and system call
tracing.
.PP
The requests are:
.TP
.B PTRACE_TRACEME
The caller asks to be traced by its parent.  It stops with
.B SIGTRAP
when it next executes a program.
.TP
.B PTRACE_ATTACH
Stop
.I pid
and become its tracer.  A process that is asleep in a system call stops
there and resumes the call when it is continued.
.TP
.BR PTRACE_PEEKTEXT ", " PTRACE_PEEKDATA
Return the word at
.I addr
in the tracee.
.TP
.BR PTRACE_POKETEXT ", " PTRACE_POKEDATA
Store the word
.I data
at
.I addr
in the tracee.
.TP
.BR PTRACE_GETREGS ", " PTRACE_SETREGS
Copy the tracee's general registers to or from the
.B struct user_regs_struct
that
.I data
points to.
.TP
.BR PTRACE_GETXSTATE ", " PTRACE_SETXSTATE
Copy the tracee's floating-point and vector registers (x87, SSE, AVX and
whatever else the system saves) to or from the buffer at
.IR data ,
in the layout of the CPU's XSAVE area.
.I addr
is the buffer's length, which must be the
.I xsave_len
that
.B PTRACE_GETXSTATE_INFO
reports.
.TP
.B PTRACE_GETXSTATE_INFO
Store in the
.B struct ptrace_xstate_info
at
.I data
the components the XSAVE area holds
.RI ( xsave_mask ,
the value of XCR0) and its size
.RI ( xsave_len ).
.TP
.BR PTRACE_GETFPXREGS ", " PTRACE_SETFPXREGS
Copy the x87 and SSE registers to or from the
.BR PTRACE_FPXREGS_SIZE -byte
buffer at
.IR data ,
in the FXSAVE layout.
.TP
.BR PTRACE_GETFPREGS ", " PTRACE_SETFPREGS
Copy the x87 registers to or from the
.BR PTRACE_FPREGS_SIZE -byte
buffer at
.IR data ,
in the FNSAVE layout.  Only on a CPU without FXSAVE.
.TP
.BR PTRACE_CONT ", " PTRACE_SINGLESTEP
Resume the tracee, to its next stop or for one instruction.
.TP
.B PTRACE_DETACH
Stop tracing the tracee and resume it.
.TP
.B PTRACE_KILL
Terminate the tracee.
.PP
A word is one
.BR long :
4 bytes for a 32-bit tracer, 8 for a 64-bit one.
.B struct user_regs_struct
likewise follows the tracer: the i386 register set for a 32-bit tracer,
and for a 64-bit one the x86-64 set (r15 through gs, with the thread
pointer in
.IR fs_base ),
in which a 32-bit tracee's registers appear zero-extended.
.PP
.B PTRACE_SETREGS
sets the general registers, the instruction and
stack pointers and the arithmetic, direction and trap flags.  The
segment registers and the remaining flags keep the tracee's values.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success,
.BR ptrace ()
returns a value that depends on the request. On error, \-1 is returned, and
.I errno
is set appropriately.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EPERM
The specified process cannot be traced.
.TP
.B ESRCH
The specified process does not exist, or the caller is not its tracer.
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I addr
or
.I data
is not a valid address, or the tracee is not stopped.
.TP
.B EIO
.B PTRACE_SETREGS
was given an instruction pointer, stack pointer or thread pointer that
the tracee could not resume with.
.TP
.B EIO
The CPU does not save its floating-point state in the layout the request
names: no XSAVE, no FXSAVE, or, for
.BR PTRACE_GETFPREGS ,
a CPU that has FXSAVE.
.TP
.B EINVAL
The request is not one of those above, or the length given to
.B PTRACE_GETXSTATE
or
.B PTRACE_SETXSTATE
is not the size of the XSAVE area.
.SH CONFORMING TO
SVr4, 4.3BSD.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gdb (1),
.BR strace (1)
.SH COLOPHON
This page is part of the Substrate operating system documentation.
